<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Document</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  body {
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  th, td {
    padding: 8px;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .header-info {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }
  .logo-area {
    text-align: left;
  }
  .contact-area {
    text-align: right;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <div class="header-info">
    <div class="logo-area">
      <h1><span data-field="organization_name">{{ organization_name }}</span></h1>
      <h2><span data-field="institute_name">{{ institute_name }}</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="contact-area">
      <p>Center for American Women and Politics</p>
      <p><span data-field="organization_address_line1">{{ organization_address_line1 }}</span></p>
      <p><span data-field="organization_address_line2">{{ organization_address_line2 }}</span></p>
      <p><span data-field="organization_address_line3">{{ organization_address_line3 }}</span></p>
      <p>www.<span data-field="organization_website">{{ organization_website }}</span></p>
      <p>Contact: <span data-field="contact_name">{{ contact_name }}</span></p>
      <p>Phone: <span data-field="contact_phone">{{ contact_phone }}</span></p>
      <p>Fax: <span data-field="contact_fax">{{ contact_fax }}</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>February 25, <span data-field="current_year">{{ current_year }}</span></p>
  <p>For immediate release</p>

  <h2>Help Wanted: More Women Needed in NJ County and Municipal Elected Offices</h2>

  <p>If New Jersey counties were graded on their efforts to elect women as freeholders, only four would receive excellent marks, and three would flunk. Progress on electing women mayors is even worse, with just two counties exceeding 25 percent, and the rest below 20 percent.</p>

  <p>These are the findings of the Center for American Women and Politics (CAWP), a unit of the Eagleton Institute of Politics at Rutgers University. CAWP compiled data on both numbers and percentages of women freeholders and mayors in New Jersey's 21 counties. (<a href="#" data-field="detailed_tables_link">{{ detailed_tables_link }}</a>)</p>

  <h3>Proportion of Women Freeholders by County</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>County</th>
        <th>Total Freeholders</th>
        <th>Women Freeholders</th>
        <th>%</th>
        <th>Rank</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for county_data in county_freeholders %}
      <tr>
        <td><span data-field="county_freeholders[{{ loop.index0 }}].county_name">{{ county_data.county_name }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="county_freeholders[{{ loop.index0 }}].total_freeholders">{{ county_data.total_freeholders }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="county_freeholders[{{ loop.index0 }}].women_freeholders">{{ county_data.women_freeholders }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="county_freeholders[{{ loop.index0 }}].percentage">{{ county_data.percentage }}%</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="county_freeholders[{{ loop.index0 }}].rank">{{ county_data.rank }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Proportion of Women Mayors by County</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>County</th>
        <th>Total Mayors</th>
        <th>Women Mayors</th>
        <th>%</th>
        <th>Rank</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for county_data in county_mayors %}
      <tr>
        <td><span data-field="county_mayors[{{ loop.index0 }}].county_name">{{ county_data.county_name }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="county_mayors[{{ loop.index0 }}].total_mayors">{{ county_data.total_mayors }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="county_mayors[{{ loop.index0 }}].women_mayors">{{ county_data.women_mayors }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="county_mayors[{{ loop.index0 }}].percentage">{{ county_data.percentage }}%</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="county_mayors[{{ loop.index0 }}].rank">{{ county_data.rank }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>At the mayoral level, only in Mercer County (33.3%) and Warren County (27.3%) are women more than a quarter of all mayors. Cumberland and Salem Counties have no women among their mayors, and the remaining counties have between 4.5% and 19.0% women mayors.</p>

  <p>"New Jersey has made significant strides in recent years at the state legislative level, where we're now 11% in the county for women's representation," noted CAWP director Debbie Walsh. "Unfortunately, at the county and municipal levels, women are still largely missing from the picture. To have reasonable balance at the county and local levels, more women must run, and both parties must do their part to create government that better reflects the population."</p>

  <p>Stone Harbor Mayor Suzanne Walters recognizes the importance of women's representation, serving in a borough where women hold the majority of council seats as well as the mayor's office. Walters, who just completed a term as president of the New Jersey League of Municipalities, observes, "Women in Stone Harbor and across the state bring distinctive talents and experiences to government. We need their voices and leadership to make our towns and counties work for everyone."</p>

  <p>Walsh invited Garden State women to learn more about running by attending Ready to Run®, CAWP's non-partisan campaign training for women, which takes place March 13-14 in New Brunswick. "Many talented women across the state haven't considered running or don't know how to explore that option," she commented. "Ready to Run® will give them essential tools to take the next steps."</p>

  <p>Information and registration is available on the <a href="#" data-field="cawp_website_link">{{ cawp_website_link }}</a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="page">
  <p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 50px;">- Page 1 of 2 -</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>